    "tree_id": "4a8ce2ceaf36eda1a0a73ca0f0f33111116d624e",
    "message": "Start a configuration's settings as a run of the stage uses them\n\nbenchmarks.md now has New benchmark run start each configuration's\nmodel, effort and session-timeout as a run of the stage uses them when\nthe dialog opens, show a model or effort nothing sets as \"Default\", and\nleave out of the configuration a setting left as it started or emptied.\n\nserve publishes each task stage's settings from the poll that gives the\nbriefs, and the benchmark page streams them beside the briefs' texts:\nthe script starts a configuration it adds from the settings as the\ndialog opened. Each setting carries the value it started with in a\nhidden cN.started-KEY field, as files of the brief do, so a poll while\nthe dialog is open cannot turn an untouched setting into an override,\nand a refused form shows its starts unchanged. A session timeout that\nis not a duration is refused as \"A session timeout is a duration, such\nas 6h.\"\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
    "timestamp": "2026-11-22T08:45:17Z",
